# Working documents, not deliverables. They hold competitor analysis, local
# filesystem paths, references to the private application this was extracted
# from, and draft launch posts.
#
# Ignored from the very first commit on purpose: a public repository keeps its
# history, so "we'll strip it later" is not a thing.
#
# The whole folder is out for now, deliberately. When a document is written to
# be READ by strangers — docs/FORMAT.md is the one that is planned — un-ignore
# that file explicitly rather than opening the folder back up.
docs/

# The working agreement for agents editing this repo. Useful, and not secret,
# but it currently points at the private specs above and reads like notes to
# self. It ships once it is written for an audience.
CLAUDE.md

# Real-world fixtures. Third-party .als files are commercial content and never
# belong here; public fixtures are synthetic or reduced, and live under
# test/fixtures.
*.als
!test/fixtures/**/*.als
